license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Milne, Jennings and Rudolph (Phys. Rev. A 92, 012311 (2015), arXiv:1407.8440, Section IV D) conjectured that, for an ellipsoid E* in the Bloch ball and the set S of two-qubit entanglement witnesses whose ellipsoid lies inside E*, the optimal witnesses in S are represented by E*. This conjecture is proved as stated: every optimal witness in S has ellipsoid E*. The stronger reading that every witness with ellipsoid E* is optimal is false: for 0 < p < 1/2 the witnesses W_p and W_{1-p} of Example 2 of the same paper share a full-dimensional Class D ellipsoid while W_{1-p} is strictly finer. For a full-dimensional target the optimal witnesses are exactly the right-handed representatives; for a planar target, all representatives. A Lean 4 development checks the counterexample for genuine complex matrices and every 0 < p < 1/2, with further ingredients; the general classification is a conventional proof using published decomposability and normal-form theorems. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
